{"drafts":[{"assumptions":["ASM-1 and ASM-14: availability notices use fixed-template email only; SMS and push notifications are excluded.","ASM-2 and ASM-12: integration uses the existing LPR camera and indicator through their supported interfaces; the vendor and interface remain to be identified.","ASM-3 and ASM-13: entrance verification fails closed with no automatic green authorization; the specified manual verification or denial procedure is handled by security outside the product.","ASM-5: English-only, left-to-right content.","ASM-6: support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.","ASM-7: WCAG 2.1 AA applies to main flows.","ASM-8: parking flows are online-only.","ASM-9: light mode only.","ASM-10: capacity assumption is up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year; no peak concurrent-claim number is established.","ASM-11: record permanent-sticker plate detections for utilization, without using them to authorize or block entry.","ASM-15: employees cannot cancel temporary claims in Phase 1.","ASM-16: a self-registered plate becomes active immediately.","ASM-18: designated report recipients are represented by a configured recipient list; the assumption text does not specify a recipient-management mechanism.","The utilization-percentage formula is not established by ASM-4 or ASM-17; the report includes a percentage field, but its calculation needs confirmation."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"0 horizontal overflow at 320, 768, and 1440 CSS-pixel viewport widths; touch targets are at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels.","text":"The product is one responsive web app with layouts for phone, tablet, and desktop; all pages avoid horizontal overflow at representative widths and narrow layouts use touch-sized controls."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"8 supported browser/version combinations: 2 versions × 4 browsers.","text":"The responsive web app supports the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"WCAG conformance level 2.1 AA for 100% of the main flows.","text":"The main flows conform to WCAG 2.1 AA."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"Up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year.","text":"The first-year deployment supports the assumed employee and record population."},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"1 supported language and 1 text direction.","text":"The responsive web app provides English, left-to-right content only."},{"id":"NFR-6","metric":"0 parking flows supported offline; 1 visual color mode.","text":"Parking flows require an online connection and the app provides light mode only."}],"outOfScope":["Native iOS or Android applications, app-store distribution, native push notifications, background location, and native home-screen behavior; the product is a responsive web app, with email used for availability notifications (ASM-1, ASM-14).","SMS notifications (ASM-1, ASM-14).","Custom report builder (ASM-4, ASM-17).","Offline parking flows (ASM-8)."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"A valid Folio3 Google Workspace identity and a personal Gmail or other non-Folio3 identity are available for sign-in tests","id":"AC-REQ-1.1","level":"api","then":"the Folio3 identity receives a successful response and each non-Folio3 identity receives a non-success response","when":"each identity submits a sign-in request"},{"given":"An employee has a successful returning-user authentication","id":"AC-REQ-1.2","level":"manual","then":"the screen shows the employee dashboard","when":"the employee opens the application"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking web app shall authenticate employees only through Folio3 Google Workspace accounts and reject personal Gmail accounts and other non-Folio3 identities.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1"],"stability":0.96},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The corporate directory and initially loaded parking roster contain an employee, an assigned-parking status, and vehicle details","id":"AC-REQ-2.1","level":"api","then":"the returned profile fields include the employee ID, employee name, assigned-parking status, assigned floor, and registered plate and vehicle details from those sources","when":"the employee profile is retrieved after sign-in"},{"given":"An administrator adds or updates an employee assignment in the roster","id":"AC-REQ-2.2","level":"api","then":"the returned profile fields reflect the roster update","when":"the employee profile is retrieved"}],"ears":"When an employee signs in, the Folio3 parking web app shall retrieve the employee profile by corporate email from the corporate directory and populate parking assignments and registered vehicle details from the administrator-maintained roster, including an initial load from existing records.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-4"],"stability":0.9},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An employee without dedicated parking has no registered vehicle","id":"AC-REQ-3.1","level":"api","then":"the response rejects the claim and the response field identifies vehicle registration as required","when":"the employee attempts a claim before registering a plate"},{"given":"An employee submits a plate with optional make, model, and color","id":"AC-REQ-3.2","level":"api","then":"the returned vehicle record contains the plate and submitted optional fields, and the plate is eligible for a parking claim","when":"the employee registers the vehicle"},{"given":"An employee without a registered vehicle opens the first-login flow","id":"AC-REQ-3.3","level":"manual","then":"the screen displays a required license-plate registration step","when":"the registration step is shown"}],"ears":"If an employee without dedicated parking has no registered vehicle, then the Folio3 parking web app shall require registration of at least one license plate before enabling claims, permit one or more registered plates with optional make, model, and color, and activate each newly registered plate immediately.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-16"],"stability":0.94},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A date range includes Monday through Sunday and a weekday holiday","id":"AC-REQ-4.1","level":"api","then":"the returned date values mark Monday through Friday, including the holiday, as working days and Saturday and Sunday as non-working days","when":"the system evaluates default working-day availability"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking web app shall treat Monday through Friday as working days, including holidays, when applying default dedicated-parking availability and utilization scenarios.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-4","I-6","Q-7"],"stability":0.94},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authenticated employee has dedicated parking that is not yet released or claimed today","id":"AC-REQ-5.1","level":"api","then":"the response confirms the release and the returned status value is Released","when":"the employee submits a release request"},{"given":"A dedicated holder is viewing the home screen and today's parking is reserved","id":"AC-REQ-5.2","level":"manual","then":"the screen shows a single release action and displays the updated parking status","when":"the holder performs the release action"},{"given":"Today's assigned space has already been released","id":"AC-REQ-5.3","level":"api","then":"the response rejects the duplicate request and the returned status value remains unchanged","when":"the holder submits another release request for today"},{"given":"A dedicated parking holder, an employee without dedicated parking, and a claimed release are available for authorization tests","id":"AC-REQ-5.4","level":"api","then":"the response permits the dedicated holder's eligible release and rejects releases by the other employee or for the already-claimed space","when":"each employee submits a release request"}],"ears":"If a dedicated parking holder releases today's assigned space, then the Folio3 parking web app shall accept the release in one action, reject a duplicate release for that date, and expose the space status as Reserved, Released, or Claimed.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2"],"stability":0.95},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A dedicated holder selects dates within the next 30 calendar days","id":"AC-REQ-6.1","level":"api","then":"the response contains a saved release record for each selected date","when":"the holder submits a schedule request"},{"given":"A dedicated holder selects a date beyond the 30-day scheduling window","id":"AC-REQ-6.2","level":"api","then":"the response rejects the out-of-window date","when":"the holder submits the schedule request"},{"given":"A dedicated holder has saved future releases","id":"AC-REQ-6.3","level":"manual","then":"the screen displays the saved release dates","when":"the holder opens the release calendar"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking web app shall allow dedicated parking holders to schedule one or more parking releases on dates up to 30 calendar days ahead and display saved releases on a calendar.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-2"],"stability":0.94},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A scheduled release has not been claimed","id":"AC-REQ-7.1","level":"api","then":"the response confirms cancellation and the returned audit list contains both the scheduling and cancellation events","when":"the holder cancels it"},{"given":"A scheduled release has already been claimed","id":"AC-REQ-7.2","level":"api","then":"the response rejects the cancellation and the returned release record remains claimed","when":"the holder attempts to cancel it"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking web app shall allow a dedicated parking holder to cancel a scheduled release only while that date's space has not been claimed and shall record each scheduling and cancellation event.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3"],"stability":0.93},{"acceptance":[{"given":"No administrator has changed the daily release time","id":"AC-REQ-8.1","level":"api","then":"the returned value is 8:00 AM in the configured office timezone","when":"the release-time configuration is read"},{"given":"An administrator submits a new daily release time","id":"AC-REQ-8.2","level":"api","then":"the response confirms the saved time and the returned value matches the configured time","when":"the configuration is saved and read back"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking web app shall use 8:00 AM as the default daily parking release time and allow an administrator to configure that time in the office's local timezone.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-2"],"stability":0.92},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The configured office timezone differs from the test client's timezone and the test clock is near a date boundary","id":"AC-REQ-9.1","level":"api","then":"the response date values match the configured office-local date boundaries","when":"the system evaluates today's date and the scheduling window"},{"given":"A report job is scheduled near the start of Monday in the office timezone","id":"AC-REQ-9.2","level":"job","then":"the job event records a Monday-morning run according to the configured office-local time","when":"the job scheduler evaluates its run time"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking web app shall evaluate today, the 30-day scheduling window, daily release cutoffs, and weekly report scheduling using the configured office-local timezone.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","I-4","I-6","Q-2"],"stability":0.94},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A future release or a same-day release before the configured daily release time is scheduled","id":"AC-REQ-10.1","level":"api","then":"the availability response includes the released space","when":"the office-local clock reaches the daily release time"},{"given":"A dedicated holder releases today's space after the configured daily release time","id":"AC-REQ-10.2","level":"api","then":"the response indicates that the space is available immediately","when":"the release request completes"}],"ears":"When a scheduled release reaches the daily release time or a same-day release occurs after that time, the Folio3 parking web app shall make the space available for claiming; a same-day release before that time shall become available at the daily release time.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-2"],"stability":0.94},{"acceptance":[{"given":"One space is available and two eligible employees submit claims concurrently","id":"AC-REQ-11.1","level":"api","then":"exactly one response confirms a claim, the other response rejects it, and the returned available-space count is zero","when":"the claim requests are processed"},{"given":"An eligible employee opens the parking availability view","id":"AC-REQ-11.2","level":"manual","then":"the screen displays the current available-space count","when":"spaces are available"},{"given":"An employee with dedicated parking submits a temporary-space claim","id":"AC-REQ-11.3","level":"api","then":"the response rejects the claim","when":"the claim request is processed"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking web app shall provide available-space counts and allocate each available space to the first eligible non-dedicated employee whose claim is accepted, allowing each space to be claimed only once.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4"],"stability":0.95},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An employee has multiple registered vehicles and an available space exists","id":"AC-REQ-12.1","level":"api","then":"the returned allocation record contains the selected plate as the only authorized plate and the assigned floor has the greatest remaining capacity, subject to the configured consistent tie-break","when":"the employee claims the space using one selected vehicle"},{"given":"An employee has a successful temporary claim","id":"AC-REQ-12.2","level":"manual","then":"the screen displays the assigned parking floor","when":"the employee views the allocation"},{"given":"An employee submits a temporary claim without selecting a registered vehicle","id":"AC-REQ-12.3","level":"api","then":"the response rejects the claim and the response field identifies vehicle selection as required","when":"the claim is processed"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking web app shall require an employee claiming temporary parking to select one registered vehicle, authorize only that vehicle's plate for the allocation, and assign a floor with the most remaining capacity using a consistent tie-break when floors have equal remaining capacity.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","I-5","Q-1","Q-3"],"stability":0.95},{"acceptance":[{"given":"At least one parking space becomes available and eligible non-dedicated employees have email addresses","id":"AC-REQ-13.1","level":"api","then":"the outbound email-service call contains the eligible recipients and a fixed-template message","when":"the availability notification is processed"}],"ears":"When one or more parking spaces become available, the Folio3 parking web app shall send an email notification using a fixed template to eligible employees without dedicated parking.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","ASM-1","ASM-14"],"stability":0.9},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An employee has an active temporary parking claim","id":"AC-REQ-14.1","level":"api","then":"the response rejects the request and the returned claim record remains active","when":"the employee submits a cancellation request"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking web app shall reject employee cancellation of a temporary parking claim in Phase 1.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","ASM-15"],"stability":0.9},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A detected car plate has a valid temporary allocation for the office-local date","id":"AC-REQ-15.1","level":"api","then":"the outbound indicator call requests green activation and the response reports an authorized result","when":"the entrance verification interface processes the detection"},{"given":"A detected car plate has no valid temporary allocation for the office-local date","id":"AC-REQ-15.2","level":"api","then":"the outbound indicator call does not request green activation and the response reports an unauthorized result","when":"the entrance verification interface processes the detection"},{"given":"The LPR camera reports a pedestrian, motorcycle, or other non-car object","id":"AC-REQ-15.3","level":"api","then":"the response contains no parking authorization result and no green-activation call is sent","when":"the detection is processed"}],"ears":"For each car plate detection received from the existing entrance LPR camera, the Folio3 parking web app shall verify the temporary allocation for that day and activate the green indicator only for a valid authorization, leaving the indicator off otherwise.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-2","ASM-12"],"stability":0.9},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A permanent-sticker vehicle detection is received, including when its dedicated holder released the space and another employee claimed it","id":"AC-REQ-16.1","level":"api","then":"a detection row is recorded and no temporary-authorization decision or entry-blocking call is made for that vehicle","when":"the detection is processed"},{"given":"A security guard checks an entrance result","id":"AC-REQ-16.2","level":"manual","then":"the screen displays only the indicator result and exposes no parking records or product screen","when":"the guard-facing surface is accessed"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking web app shall record permanent-sticker vehicle plate detections for utilization, bypass temporary authorization and entry blocking for those detections, and limit guard-facing product access to the indicator result.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-6","Q-6","Q-8","ASM-11"],"stability":0.9},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An entrance check encounters a camera, recognition, network, or indicator failure, or an unreadable plate","id":"AC-REQ-17.1","level":"api","then":"the response reports an unsuccessful result, the verification row records the failure, and no green-activation call is issued","when":"the verification interface processes the failure"}],"ears":"If the camera, plate recognition, network, or indicator fails or a plate cannot be read during an entrance check, then the Folio3 parking web app shall issue no automatic green authorization and shall record an unsuccessful verification result for manual verification handling.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-3","ASM-13"],"stability":0.84},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A dedicated holder did not release a working-day space and no registered vehicle entry exists for that date","id":"AC-REQ-18.1","level":"job","then":"a utilization row records Unused Dedicated Parking with the employee, vehicle, and date fields","when":"the utilization evaluation runs"},{"given":"An employee claimed temporary parking and the selected vehicle has no entry detection on the claim date","id":"AC-REQ-18.2","level":"job","then":"a utilization row records Unused Temporary Parking with the employee, vehicle, and date fields","when":"the utilization evaluation runs"},{"given":"A permanent-sticker vehicle enters the facility","id":"AC-REQ-18.3","level":"api","then":"the detection row is available to the utilization evaluation","when":"its entry detection is processed for utilization"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking web app shall record an Unused Dedicated Parking event for each working day when a dedicated holder did not release the space and no registered vehicle entry was detected, and an Unused Temporary Parking event when a claimant's selected vehicle was not detected entering on the claim date.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","Q-7","Q-1"],"stability":0.91},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Utilization history exists for the reporting week","id":"AC-REQ-19.1","level":"job","then":"the generated report file contains the dedicated-unused and temporary-unused employee lists, daily and weekly statistics, released-space count, temporary-claim count, and an overall utilization-percentage field","when":"the Monday-morning report job runs"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking web app shall generate a weekly utilization report every Monday morning in the office timezone containing dedicated employees who neither released nor used their parking, temporary claimants who did not use their parking, daily and weekly utilization statistics, total released spaces, total temporary claims, and an overall utilization percentage.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","Q-2","ASM-4","ASM-17"],"stability":0.84},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A weekly report is generated and designated stakeholder email addresses are configured","id":"AC-REQ-20.1","level":"job","then":"the outbound email-service call contains the stakeholder recipients and the generated report","when":"the report email job runs"},{"given":"An administrator changes the designated stakeholder recipient list","id":"AC-REQ-20.2","level":"api","then":"the returned recipient list contains the updated addresses","when":"the list is read for the next report"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking web app shall email each weekly utilization report to the designated stakeholders using the configured stakeholder recipient list.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","ASM-18"],"stability":0.88},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A utilization evaluation identifies unused dedicated or temporary parking","id":"AC-REQ-21.1","level":"job","then":"no warning, suspension, or penalty row, event, email, or outbound enforcement call is created","when":"the evaluation and report jobs run"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking web app shall not create automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties based on parking utilization in Phase 1.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6"],"stability":0.95},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A test retention policy is configured for release, claim, LPR verification, and utilization history","id":"AC-REQ-22.1","level":"job","then":"the row list retains in-period records and removes or archives expired records according to the policy","when":"the retention job runs across records both within and beyond the configured retention period"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking web app shall retain release, claim, LPR verification, and utilization history according to Folio3's existing records-retention policy.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","I-4","I-5","I-6","Q-5"],"stability":0.83}],"suggestions":["Confirm the utilization-percentage numerator and denominator before implementation so report percentages can be tested for correctness.","Identify the existing LPR camera and indicator vendor, supported interfaces, failure codes, and integration test environment.","Resolve and document the security procedure for an unreadable plate or an unavailable camera, network, or indicator.","Confirm how designated report recipients are administered and whether filtered lists or CSV export are in scope.","Confirm whether reporting is expected to include an on-screen list or CSV export; neither is specified in the request."]}],"models":["gpt-6-luna"],"notes":[]}